  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so the first priority is to establish a clean, minimal baseline that calibrates the search space. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest possible configuration: it uses a linear, well-understood encoder (PCA), requires no image processing or fusion, and has no aggregation complexity. This experiment will (1) confirm the pipeline runs end-to-end, (2) quantify how much signal is available from RNA data alone, and (3) set a performance floor against which all image-only and multimodal configurations can be compared. Choosing the simplest RNA baseline first is the most budget-efficient use of the first experiment because it is fast to execute (no image encoder or fusion overhead), minimizes the risk of confounding from multiple design choices, and directly informs whether the image modality or multimodal fusion is necessary to achieve strong performance. Subsequent experiments can then systematically add image modality, upgrade encoders, or test multiprofile aggregation with a clear reference point."
}

